"""Produce the scoped engineering readout only after semantic acceptance."""
import pathlib,json,collections,sys
ROOT=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4];out=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
r=json.loads((out/'results.json').read_text());sem=json.loads(pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]).read_text());assert sem['outcome']=='Pass' and sem['guards']=='Pass';assert sem['timedCapturesLinked']==13968
pre=[c for c in r['comparisons'] if c['before']=='preN9'];control=[c for c in r['comparisons'] if c['before']=='acceptedN9']
def counts(xs,m):return dict(collections.Counter(c['metrics'].get(m,{}).get('classification',c['comparison']) for c in xs))
assert counts(pre,'wallMs')=={'observed-faster':272,'no-successful-latency-comparison':36,'capacity-improved':2}
assert counts(pre,'cpuTotalMs')=={'observed-faster':194,'observed-slower':6,'inconclusive-within-observed-variation':72,'no-successful-latency-comparison':36,'capacity-improved':2}
assert len(r['cells'])==930 and len(r['comparisons'])==620
def fmt(v):return 'Not estimated' if v is None else f'{v:.3f}'
def cell(family,size,deadline,op,phase):return next(c for c in pre if (c['family'],c['size'],c['deadline'],c['operation'],c['phase'])==(family,size,deadline,op,phase))
s=['# RX-9004 — Matched native Node build/query results','', '**5 November 2026. The selected Node workload shows lower observed wall time versus pre-N9, with CPU and work tradeoffs.** All 272 matched-success wall cells have strictly separated three-owner median ranges in the faster direction. That is a scoped observation under the frozen recipe, not a universal winner or a new post-N9 optimization. Process CPU total has 194 observed-faster cells, six observed-slower cells and 72 overlapping/inconclusive cells. Two additional 10k restore cells improve from refusal to success; 36 cells have no successful latency comparison.','', 'The current implementation is byte-identical to accepted N9. Their control pair has eight faster and eight slower wall separations plus 258 overlapping cells despite identical runtime bytes. Those differences demonstrate method/environment variation; they are not further implementation gains. RX-9005 updates, RX-9006 hosts/recovery/resources and the RX-9007 combined verdict remain separate.','', '## Method and acceptance','', 'The unchanged [frozen method](RX-9001-method.md) and [Node profile](../../bench/n10/contract.mjs) execute 216 fresh serial processes: 162 normal and 54 diagnostic. They cover all nine family/size workloads, three original installed archive roles, both omitted/default30s and explicit60s options, unchanged limits, source plus source-phrase body configuration and exact totals/top20. A whole build spans multiple calls of at most 256 records, each with its own operation deadline; total build wall time may exceed 30 seconds. The recorded collection takes 6,859,873.6445ms within its declared 10,800s budget. Owner order reverses on the second repeat; this is rotation, not randomization or perfect balancing.','', 'There are 13,536 ordinary query calls, 432 separate diagnostic queries and 576 untimed warmups. Normal calls yield 11,880 successful queries and 1,656 explicit refusals; diagnostics yield 384/48. The raw collector intentionally keeps acceptedPerformanceEvidence=false until independent semantic/review gates are supplied. This readout uses those separate gates; it never rewrites the raw collector flag.','', f"The actual 27-process controlled-host semantic lane passes: {sem['totals']['completeQueries']} complete query captures, {sem['totals']['refusedQueries']} explicit refused captures, {sem['totals']['pages']} actual successful pages and {sem['totals']['sourceScores']} independently source-derived semantic score checks. It links all 13,968 timed query captures, including {sem['timedSourceScoreAssertions']} additional timed successful-score checks. Selected source statistics and Inspector formula replay, canonical core/source state, four small provider configurations per role and subsequent writes retain their exact scope. Clock-zero semantic execution is not latency, default-deadline capacity or host-fairness evidence.",'', 'Every source/archive/consumer/harness/configuration identity guard passes; all 5,498 recorded non-task inputs stay unchanged through timing. See the [task evidence](../evidence/RX-9004.md), [new run manifest](../evidence/RX-9004/identity/artifacts.json), [complete ordinary distributions/comparisons](../evidence/RX-9004/analysis/results.json), [all-cell CSV](../evidence/RX-9004/analysis/comparisons.csv) and retained raw inventories. The original RX-9001 freeze remains unchanged.','', '## Selected query distributions','', 'Adversarial 1,000 records, ordinary omitted/default30s, after two excluded warmups. Each labeled role/query has 120 actual calls across three independent process owners. All values below are milliseconds. P95 is descriptive nearest-rank across correlated calls, not a population/device tail. Process CPU total is user+system, including harness/Promise/JIT activity; user and system remain separately retained.','', '| Query | Pre wall p50 | Current wall p50 | Change | Pre/current wall p95 | Pre/current CPU total p50 | CPU range result |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |']
for q in ['common','rare','narrow-prefix','source-phrase']:
 c=cell('adversarial',1000,'default30s','query:'+q,'after-two-warmups');w=c['metrics']['wallMs'];cpu=c['metrics']['cpuTotalMs'];s.append(f"| {q} | {fmt(w['beforeP50'])} | {fmt(w['afterP50'])} | {w['relativeChangePercent']:.1f}% | {fmt(w['beforeP95'])} / {fmt(w['afterP95'])} | {fmt(cpu['beforeP50'])} / {fmt(cpu['afterP50'])} | {cpu['classification']} |")
s+=['', 'Cells include operation, phase and deadline splits; they are not independent workloads or devices. All absolute/relative changes, per-owner ranges and adverse/inconclusive rows remain in the CSV/JSON. Selected examples do not replace the complete matrix. Eighty-four successful tail cells meet the >=100 observation p95 rule; twelve additional refused-outcome cells have separately labeled refusal-cost p95 in the original raw summaries. Sparse first/repeated cells have three observations/phase, build/recovery cells three owners, and no p95 estimate.','', '## Every observed CPU regression','', 'These six process-CPU-total cells have strictly separated owner-median ranges in the slower direction. They all have lower wall time. Each has only three actual successful observations (one per owner), so p95 is Not estimated. These are retained costs, not a claim of isolated engine CPU or an explained causal stage effect.','', '| Family / size / operation | Deadline | Pre/current wall p50 | Pre/current CPU total p50 | CPU delta ms | CPU delta % |','| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
for c in pre:
 cpu=c['metrics'].get('cpuTotalMs',{})
 if cpu.get('classification')=='observed-slower':
  w=c['metrics']['wallMs'];s.append(f"| {c['family']} / {c['size']} / {c['operation']} ({c['phase']}) | {c['deadline']} | {fmt(w['beforeP50'])} / {fmt(w['afterP50'])} | {fmt(cpu['beforeP50'])} / {fmt(cpu['afterP50'])} | +{cpu['absoluteChangeMs']:.3f} | +{cpu['relativeChangePercent']:.1f}% |")
s+=['', 'These CPU increases remain unexplained at the conditional-stage level. No intermediate-stage attribution run was selected, and no speculative optimization was made. The 72 overlapping/inconclusive CPU cells also retain their actual absolute/relative changes, including unfavorable p50 movements. A positive aggregate movement alone does not satisfy the frozen separation rule.','', '## Logical work and capacity','', 'Separate adversarial-1k/default30s diagnostics observe rare-query evaluated documents 1,000→1 and emitted work 77,639→1,085; narrow-prefix visits 3,007→72 and emitted work 129,899→18,719. Common-query average-length/IDF computations fall 1,000→1 while emitted work is 304,148→304,153. Source-phrase emitted work increases 635,969→655,972 and yields 308→318 despite lower observed wall time. These are actual diagnostic counters, not ordinary timing, retained/peak heap or additive stage effects.','', 'At adversarial 10k, all six ordinary pre-N9 restore attempts refuse (three DEADLINE_EXCEEDED under default30s, three WORK_LIMIT_EXCEEDED under explicit60s); all six current attempts pass. This is capacity improvement in two declared cells, with zero equal-work speed ratio. Separate current diagnostic restores consume 23,043,299 emitted work units in each deadline cohort. Prior-state preservation after authoritative baseline refusal and complete source/revision replacement after success are verified.','', 'All 36 ordinary large real-doc/high-cardinality source exports still refuse (six deadline, thirty work), leaving 36 dependent restores Not run with zero fabricated times. Diagnostics have 12 refused exports (two deadline, ten work) and 12 dependent restores Not run. Broad-prefix and source-phrase work/expansion refusals remain explicit; no limits were raised, results approximated or refused duration treated as successful latency.','', '## Practical limits','', 'Use these results as evidence for the selected native Node source+phrase workloads: net wall-time gains coexist with process CPU and logical-work costs. The corpus labeled real-docs repeats 34 original sections; it is not 10,000 independent real documents or representative traffic. Three process owners on one recorded Apple M5 Pro/Node 24.21.0 host are not independent devices. Same-runtime variation, timer floors, sparse distributions, all refused/unavailable outcomes and full input identities remain visible.','', 'No weighted overall winner, new post-N9 runtime optimization, browser/worker gain, incremental-update distribution, retained/peak heap, physical input/paint or universal platform conclusion follows. Those later selected cohorts and the final combined verdict remain unrun. Source/runtime/tests/dependencies are unchanged; this is uncommitted local measurement evidence, not fresh exact-commit CI or publication.','']
(ROOT/'docs/evaluation/RX-9004.md').write_text('\n'.join(s))
summary={'kind':'rx9004-classifications-v1','semanticGate':'Pass','normalCells':len(r['cells']),'comparisonCells':len(r['comparisons']),'preN9ToCurrent':{m:counts(pre,m) for m in ['wallMs','cpuUserMs','cpuSystemMs','cpuTotalMs']},'sameRuntimeControl':{m:counts(control,m) for m in ['wallMs','cpuUserMs','cpuSystemMs','cpuTotalMs']},'successfulP95Cells':84,'separateRefusedP95Cells':12,'scope':'Observed three-owner median-range separation only; no overall weighted winner or additional same-runtime optimization.'}
(out/'classifications.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2)+'\n');print(json.dumps({'report':'docs/evaluation/RX-9004.md','semanticTotals':sem['totals'],'preN9CpuTotal':summary['preN9ToCurrent']['cpuTotalMs']},indent=2))
